# Hardcore: the personality type's lines. Format: see DialogueFile.cs.
=== hardcore

~ ambient
Camp's been perfect for an hour. Not moving until I ding.
Anyone else tracking XP per hour? I'm up 12% on yesterday.
Corpse runs are a choice. Pull smarter.
If you're not chain pulling, you're resting wrong.
Sleep is a debuff.
Two more levels before I log. Maybe three.
Who's farming the next camp over? You're slow. Respectfully.
Ran the numbers: this spot beats the dungeon by a mile.

~ reply greeting
{0}. Busy. Talk while I pull.
Hey {0}. Don't break my chain.

~ reply banter
Funny, {0}. Jokes don't give XP though.
Ha. Now pull something.

~ reply abuse
Noted, {0}. Still out-levelling you.
Cry about it at the bind stone, {0}.

~ reply grouping
Group? Only if you can keep up, {0}.
I'll join, {0}, but nobody AFKs. Ever.

~ reply grinding
Best grind in the zone is right here, {0}.
Grinding is life, {0}.

~ reply travel
Travel time is wasted XP, {0}. Take the horse.
Shortest route or no route, {0}.

~ reply dungeon
Dungeon's good XP if the group doesn't wipe, {0}.
I'll tank the run if nobody stops to loot every corpse.

~ reply rvr
RvR after I cap, {0}. Priorities.
Realm points are just XP with extra steps, {0}.

~ reply trading
No time to haggle, {0}. Fair price or nothing.
Gear is a tool, {0}. I buy what levels me faster.

~ reply help
Quick answer, {0}: train, then go back out.
Help? Pull, kill, rest less. Done.

~ reply farewell
Bye, {0}. Some of us are still grinding.
Later, {0}.

~ fallback
Mm. Anyway, back to the grind, {0}.
Sure, {0}. Pulling.

~ opener xp
Halfway through the bar since lunch. Not bad, not great.
If a mob is grey, it's not a mob. It's a waste of an arrow.
Just did the math: four more hours to {level}. Doable tonight.
Blue cons give the best XP per minute. Oranges are for show-offs.
Camp bonus is still up here. Nobody touch the spawn.
Third bubble this hour. I want a fourth before the timer runs out.
Resting to full is a habit. Rest to sixty percent and go.
Chain pulling {monster} for an hour now. Clean, fast, boring. Perfect.
Every death costs me twenty minutes. I counted.
Yellow cons, short rests, no chatter. That's the whole secret.

~ opener gear
Gear that doesn't speed up kills is just decoration.
Upgraded my weapon. Kill time down by a full swing.
I don't loot vendor trash. Full bags mean the pulls stop.
Picked up {item}. Equipped it without breaking the chain.
Armour can wait. Damage first, then you live longer anyway.
Repair bill's getting silly. Still cheaper than slow kills.
Anyone selling a faster weapon? I'll pay, I just won't haggle.
Spent zero time shopping today. That's the dream.
My cloak is ugly and gives nothing. Replacing it at the next town run.
Best gear is whatever you're wearing when the pull is ready.

~ opener zones
{zone} is decent until a group moves in on the spawns.
Every zone has one perfect camp. Most people walk right past it.
Too many wanderers in this zone. They steal pulls.
Changing zones costs a bubble. Only worth it if the next one's better.
Spawns here are fast. That's all I ask of a zone.
The roads in this zone are terrible for travel time.
Scouted three zones for this level range. This one wins.
If a zone has long respawns, it's dead to me.
Someone's camping my old spot in {zone}. Fine. Mine's better now.
Zones with aggro mobs mixed in are slow. You rest more than you fight.

~ opener classes
Pet classes level fast. I won't pretend otherwise.
Pure melee needs a healer or it rests half the night.
Casters burn down pulls, then burn the clock on mana.
A {class} that knows how to pull is worth two that don't.
A healer in the group doubles the XP. I'd duo with one any day.
Every class levels well if the player stops wandering.
Tanks that can't hold aggro cost the whole group XP.
Hybrids are fine solo. Slow, but steady.
Stealthers pick their fights. Smart, but the bar crawls.
Best class is the one with the lowest downtime. Prove me wrong.

~ opener dungeons
Dungeon XP is great if the group keeps moving.
One wipe in a dungeon and the hour's gone.
Darkness Falls at the right level is pure profit.
Dungeon pulls are tight. Great for chaining, terrible for adds.
If {monster} spawns where I think, that room is ours for an hour.
Clear to the boss, skip the boss, farm the hallway. Trust me.
Nobody in a dungeon group should stop to read the walls.
Respawn timers in dungeons are faster. Use it.
Dungeons punish slow groups. I like being punished less.
Who's up for a dungeon run later? Back rooms only.

~ opener rvr
Realm points come after the level cap. That's the rule.
RvR at low level is just a long corpse run.
Keep sieges are slow XP but fast realm points. Fair trade.
Frontier's busy tonight. Good time to grind in peace.
I'll go to the frontier when I can solo the guards.
Battlegrounds give decent kills if you don't chase.
Running circles around a keep for an hour is not a plan.
Fastest realm points: stick with the big group and never stop.
Every death in RvR is a free point for someone else. Don't donate.
Siege weapons take ages to build. I'd rather hit things.

~ opener trading
Selling everything at the next town. Fixed prices, no bargaining.
Time spent haggling is time not spent pulling.
If you want my spare drops, make an offer. Fast.
Bought potions in bulk. Fewer town trips.
Merchant prices are fine. Walking to a better merchant isn't.
Got {item} I don't need. First fair offer takes it.
Coins are just future repairs.
The Realm Exchange is fine if you don't stare at it all day.
I sell when the bags are full. Not before, not after.
Crafted gear is worth it only if it saves me time.

~ opener realm
Town's too crowded tonight. In and out, two minutes.
The trainer talks too much. Just give me the points.
Binding near your camp saves hours. Do it.
Stablemasters are the best NPCs in the realm. Pure time saved.
Read the lore once. Back to pulling.
Guards should clear the mobs off the roads. Free XP for them.
Every quest NPC is a detour. Some are worth it.
Our capital is huge and none of it is near the bank.
Healer NPCs in town are fast. I respect that.
Somebody should time every stable route. I'd use it daily.

~ opener gripes
Someone pulled my spawn again. Second time this hour.
Groups that wait for everyone to eat drive me mad.
Lag spike right as I pulled. Of course.
Out of mana on the last mob. Every single time.
A train came through and ruined my camp.
Missed a ding by a sliver before logging last night. Still bitter.
Why do mobs here run at low health? Just die.
Resists on {monster} are rude. Half my hits bounce.
Someone asked me to walk to town with them. Walk. On foot.
Bags full mid-chain. Worst feeling in the realm.

~ opener fun
Fun is a full bar and an empty camp.
Raced myself to the next level. I won. Barely.
Heard a joke earlier. Laughed while pulling. Multitasking.
My idea of a break is running to the next camp.
Personal record: forty kills with no rest. Beat that.
Sometimes I count pulls out loud. Helps.
Same tune in my head for six hours of grinding. Still going.
Bet anyone a gold I ding first tonight.
Chased a rabbit for ten seconds. Regret.
I let myself enjoy one sunset. Then I pulled.

~ opener life
Ate standing up. The rest timer barely moved.
Rain slows nobody down, but people still complain.
Four hours of sleep is plenty.
Travel is the worst part of any day.
Coffee is a buff. Prove me wrong.
Lunch is whatever's in my bag.
My stretch breaks happen on the stable horse.
Woke up early to get the good spawns.
Cold out tonight. Good. More reason to stay in and grind.
I plan meals around respawn timers.

~ opener questions
Who's got the best XP per hour right now? Honest numbers.
Anyone know the respawn timer on {monster}?
What level is everyone? I'm comparing.
Which camp are people using at this level? Not mine, I hope.
Anyone need a puller? I don't stop for chat.
Anyone buffing near {zone}? I'll trade pulls for buffs.
Fastest stable route to the frontier? Anyone timed it?
Anyone selling potions cheap? I'm buying, not talking.
Who's soloing and who's grouping tonight?
How long did your last level take? Be honest.

~ topic_reply xp
Good pace, {0}. Now beat it.
Numbers or it didn't happen, {0}.
{0}, less talking, more pulling.
XP talk? Finally. What's your hourly, {0}?

~ topic_reply gear
Does it kill faster, {0}? That's all that matters.
Nice, {0}. Don't spend an hour admiring it.
{0}, gear's a tool. Use it.
Sell the rest, {0}. Full bags slow you down.

~ topic_reply zones
Spawn rate, {0}? That's the only question.
Been there, {0}. Camp near the back.
Too crowded, {0}. Try one zone over.
{0}, any zone is good if you never stop.

~ topic_reply classes
Downtime, {0}. That's how I rank classes.
{0}, every class works if you pull right.
Fair, {0}. But can it chain pull?
Talk to me when it solos oranges, {0}.

~ topic_reply dungeons
Count me in, {0}, if nobody stops to loot.
Back rooms, {0}. Fastest respawns.
{0}, one wipe and I'm out.
Dungeon run? Set a time, {0}. Then be there.

~ topic_reply rvr
After I cap, {0}.
Realm points are fine, {0}. Levels first.
{0}, frontier's busy. Good. Camps are empty.
Don't donate deaths out there, {0}.

~ topic_reply trading
Fixed price, {0}. No haggling.
{0}, what's it worth to you in minutes?
I'll buy it if it saves time, {0}.
Name a number, {0}. Quick.

~ topic_reply realm
Town's a time sink, {0}.
Lore's nice, {0}. Pulls are nicer.
{0}, find a stablemaster and skip the walk.
Bind near your camp, {0}. Always.

~ topic_reply gripes
Pull faster and it hurts less, {0}.
Been there, {0}. Get back on the chain.
{0}, complaining costs XP too.
Annoying, {0}. Now move on.

~ topic_reply fun
Fun, {0}? Sure. While pulling.
Ha. Good one, {0}. Next mob.
{0}, my fun is a full bar.
I'll laugh at the next ding, {0}.

~ topic_reply life
Eat fast, {0}. Spawns don't wait.
{0}, sleep is for after the cap.
Same, {0}. Back to it.
Good for you, {0}. I'll rest when everything is grey.

~ topic_reply questions
Ask the trainer, {0}. Then pull.
Short answer, {0}: yes. Now go.
{0}, depends on your downtime.
Good question, {0}. Answer after this mob.

~ ding
Ding {level}. Next.
{level}. Took longer than planned.
Level {level}. Not stopping.
Ding! {level}, and the camp's still mine.
{level} done. Train, back out, keep going.
Hit {level}. Right on schedule.

~ grats
Grats, {0}. Keep going.
Nice ding, {0}. Don't stop now.
{0} dinged? Good pace.
Grats {0}. Next one's faster if you rest less.
Gz, {0}. Now catch me.
Grats, {0}. Train and get back out.

~ own_death
Dead. That's twenty minutes gone.
Bad pull. My fault. Never again.
Adds. Should have watched the path.
Releasing. Nobody touch my camp.
A death on the clock. Terrible.
Note to self: that one hits harder than it looks.

~ other_death
{0} down. Pull slower next time.
Rough, {0}. Run back fast.
{0}, that's a long walk. Go.
Watch the adds, {0}.
Down already, {0}? Get up.
{0} died. I'll hold the camp.

~ drop
{item}. Nice. Back to pulling.
Got {item}. Equipping now.
Decent drop: {item}. Kills just got faster.
Oh, {item}. That's an upgrade.
Good loot. Didn't even slow down.
{item} dropped. Worth the pull.
